From 24673cac2e635dea0e2fcbac606e7e945ebb1552 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:28:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firewall: report engine on/off from a measured signal, and
 fix the backup box

THE TOGGLE HAD NO FEEDBACK AT ALL - the click fired action=opts with an empty
callback and the page said nothing, so a working toggle and a dead one looked
identical. Owner asked for progress text that ends in "complete".

It cannot simply announce success when the request returns. opts calls
notify_rc(), which returns as soon as rc has been SIGNALLED; the chains change
afterwards in another process, and may not change at all - the "LAN not ready at
boot" deferral is a real path where the engine is enabled and no chain exists.
Reporting an accepted request as a finished job is the inferred-signal-as-fact
mistake, which is exactly what Sentinel was rejected for. Polling reaper_fw_enable
would be no better: that is the flag opts just wrote, so it would read back
"enabled" instantly whatever rc did.

So the completion signal is now MEASURED. start_reaper_fw()/stop_reaper_fw() set
a new runtime nvram, reaper_fw_active, as their LAST act - and start sets it only
when the generated script actually RAN, not merely when it was written, so the
deferred path reports inactive rather than claiming success quietly. cfg reports
it; the page shows an animated "Working..." immediately, polls until active
matches what was asked, then states the result. If it has not converged in ~15 s
it says so and does NOT auto-hide - an operator who believes a firewall is live
when it is not is worse off than one who knows something went wrong. Success
auto-hides through the existing showSaved(), so no new styling.

reaper_fw_active is deliberately distinct from reaper_fw_enable: enable is what
was asked for, active is what is true. They differ while a restart is in flight.

ALSO, from the same review pass:

- The backup/restore textarea rendered BLINDING WHITE. The rule beside it is
  `input.fld,select.fld` and never matched a TEXTAREA, so it fell through to the
  browser default in the middle of a dark page. Given its own rule rather than
  bolted onto that selector, because the shared one carries max-width:520px and
  this box wants the full card width. Same --panel-3 as the inputs next to it
  with --bone text, so the JSON stays legible.

- The box is empty on a first visit and nothing said why. The note above it now
  tells the operator to click Export first, and a placeholder repeats it inside
  the empty box where it is actually needed. RFW_218 was REPLACED IN PLACE (same
  line, so no token index moves) and RFW_228 appended; all 25 packs, lockstep at
  6549 lines.

Verified without a build: the generator harness still compiles reaper_fw.c and
produces a correct ruleset (no cross-chain leaks, no duplicates, the four invalid
forwards still refused); every id the JS touches exists; all page tokens resolve;
reaper_langcheck 0 breakers; 125 script blocks parse in all 25 languages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
